[s0;#b17;a17; [*+139 Adding processes]&]
[s0;#b17;a17; [+93 Processes are added to BatchManager by ][*+93 drag 
and drop][+93  onto the process list, where they appear with status 
][*+93 Pending][+93 . Two types of files are supported:]&]
[s0;#l250;i93;b17;a17;O0; [*+93 Drag an executable or batch file (.exe, 
.bat) directly][+93  — it is added and run as`-is.]&]
[s0;#l250;i93;b17;a17;O0; [*+93 Drag a data file whose type is registered 
in Managed file types][+93  (see below) — BatchManager looks 
up the file`'s name and extension, and if it matches a registered 
pattern, launches the associated command with the associated 
arguments, using the dropped file`'s path to fill in the placeholders. 
This lets you, for example, drop a .dat file and have BatchManager 
automatically run the right solver on it, without having to build 
thecommand line by hand each time.]&]
