[s0;#b17;a17; [*+139 Resource constraints]&]
[s0;#b17;a17; [+93 BatchManager enforces two independent constraints. 
When either is reached, Running processes are Paused (and Pending 
ones held back) until usage drops again and resources are available.]&]
[s0;#b17;a17;+93 &]
[s0;#b17;a17; [*+108 Process Constraints]&]
[s0;#b17;a17; [+93 The ][*+93 Available][+93  slider sets the maximum number 
of processes BatchManager is allowed to run ][*+93 simultaneously][+93 . 
The text to the right shows this as `"][/+93 N][+93  processes running 
<`= ][/+93 M][+93  available`" — ][/+93 N][+93  is how many are running 
now, ][/+93 M][+93  is the current limit from the slider.]&]
[s0;#b17;a17; [+93 The checkbox next to `"Process Constraints`" presumably 
enables/disablesthis limit entirely.]&]
[s0;#b17;a17;+93 &]
[s0;#b17;a17; [*+108 Memory `[GB`] Constraints]&]
[s0;#b17;a17; [+93 The ][*+93 Available][+93  slider sets the maximum total 
memory, in GB, that BatchManager`'s processes are allowed to 
use together. The text to the right shows this as `"][/+93 The 
processes use N GB, peak of M GB < P GB available][+93 `" — ][/+93 N][+93  
is the memory currently in use by all BatchManager processes 
